# Current theses

## Thesis T-migrated-adapters-gradle: Preserve reviewed project guidance
Status: accepted
Based-on: user-reviewed-contract-migration

### Guidance
#### module Gradle checkout integration

Detect `settings.gradle.kts` before `settings.gradle` and consume the ordinary Maven export name
`group:artifact`. The lifecycle passes `Export.Path` as the consumer-root-relative directory in
the one submodule checkout. This adapter never materializes source.

#### decision Composite build substitution is generated by DSL variant

Kotlin and Groovy consumers retain distinct generated files and marked apply lines. Sorted blocks
use `includeBuild(Export.Path)` and substitute the export coordinate with project `:`. Remove
removes only the named owned block and removes the marked line only when the generated file is
empty. Foreign bytes in the wholly owned generated file are reported and canonically repaired.

#### invariant Saved Gradle variants remain explicit and resolved

`Ecosystem()` is `maven`; detection returns `gradle-kts` or `gradle-groovy`. The lifecycle stores
and verifies that concrete variant. Read-only Capability requires a Maven `group:artifact` name
and a relative non-escaping checkout path, returning typed not-wirable for unsupported shapes.
Pull requires the submodule checkout, writes the composite substitution, and runs `gradle
--no-daemon help` to resolve/configure it without building the whole consumer. Remove applies
native configuration after deleting only owned integration; Inspect reports a missing checkout.

#### test Golden lifecycle

Tests cover both DSL variants, private editor idempotence, Inspect, sorted blocks,
foreign-content repair, byte-restoring removal, read-only Capability, and missing checkouts.

### Rationale
Migrated from the pre-2.0 HINT source format without changing its guidance.

